<p dir="auto">This means:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>{<code>bbb.grd</code>, <code>bbb_helper.grd</code>} is one group.</li>
<li>{<code>bbb_testing.grd</code>, <code>bbb_testing_helper.grd</code>} is another group.</li>
<li>The two groups are mutually exclusive, and IDs can be reused.</li>
<li><code>ddd.grd</code> is used by everyone; it "joins" the mutually exclusive branches.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">If you're adding <code>foo/bar/ccc.grd</code>, and it's unrelated to <code>bbb*.grd</code> then the
required update would be:</p>
